"""Reference-as-solution wrapper for ``_cast_Byte`` (``aten::_cast_Byte``).

This file is the preparation-stage reference solution for the operator that the
frozen kernelgen-dev suite calls as ``flag_gems._cast_Byte``. It is loaded by the
official runtime injector (``--override _cast_Byte:<this file>:run``), so the
receiving ABI is exactly the candidate ABI: ``(self, non_blocking=False)``.

The oracle is the backend's native ATen operator, which is also the reference
used by the frozen master test (``torch.ops.aten._cast_Byte``). It is *not* the
current candidate: ``flag_gems`` is never imported here, and the injected
candidate is a plain ``flag_gems._cast_Byte`` attribute, so no Gems dispatch
path is re-entered and no recursion into the candidate is possible.

Keeping the native operator preserves the vendor-observable cast semantics that
the master workloads assert: uint8 inputs are returned unchanged (same object,
same device, no copy), non-uint8 inputs produce a new uint8 tensor whose layout
follows ATen ``empty_like`` Preserve semantics (so stride assertions hold), the
result never requires grad, and floating inputs follow the vendor narrowing
rules (saturating ``f32/f16/bf16/f64 -> int`` then truncation to ``uint8``),
including the fractional/out-of-range/non-finite cases in the master suite.
"""

import torch


def run(x, non_blocking=False):
    """Cast ``x`` to ``torch.uint8`` with ``aten::_cast_Byte`` semantics."""
    return torch.ops.aten._cast_Byte.default(x, non_blocking)
